---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service">
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="meta"><a href="/">← Back home</a></p>

  <h2>what beadster is</h2>
  <p>beadster is a local issue tracker for developers. manage tasks and issues stored in <code>.beads</code> folders within your projects.</p>
  <p>everything runs locally on your Mac. no cloud, no sync, no accounts.</p>

  <h2>who can use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>anyone can download and use beadster.</li>
    <li>free to use.</li>
    <li>no account required.</li>
    <li>no age restrictions (but generally aimed at developers).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>acceptable use</h2>
  <p>don't:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>reverse engineer or modify the app in ways that violate the App Store terms.</li>
    <li>use beadster to store illegal content.</li>
    <li>attempt to hack or abuse the app.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>that's it. it's your local data, your rules.</p>

  <h2>your content</h2>
  <p>you own all issue data you create in beadster.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>stored locally in your projects.</li>
    <li>we never see or access your data.</li>
    <li>no license granted to us (because we never receive your content).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>service availability</h2>
  <p>beadster is provided "as is" without warranties.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>we can't guarantee the app will be bug-free.</li>
    <li>we'll do our best to fix issues and improve the app.</li>
    <li>we may discontinue the app with reasonable notice.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>no liability for data loss</h2>
  <p>since everything is local:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>back up your projects regularly (use Time Machine, Git, etc).</li>
    <li>we're not responsible for data loss.</li>
    <li><code>.beads</code> folders are plain text files - you can back them up like any other file.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>liability</h2>
  <p>we're not liable for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>data loss or corruption.</li>
    <li>bugs or crashes.</li>
    <li>compatibility issues with your system.</li>
    <li>indirect damages or lost productivity.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>beadster is free software provided as-is.</p>
  <p>our total liability is limited to $0 (since the app is free).</p>

  <h2>updates and changes</h2>
  <p>we may:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>release updates with bug fixes and new features.</li>
    <li>change these terms (we'll notify you through app updates).</li>
    <li>discontinue the app (we'll give reasonable notice).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>continued use after updates means you accept any new terms.</p>

  <h2>future paid features</h2>
  <p>if we add paid features in the future (like cloud sync):</p>
  <ul>
    <li>current local-only features will remain free.</li>
    <li>you can continue using the free version.</li>
    <li>paid features will be clearly optional.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>termination</h2>
  <p>you can stop using beadster anytime by deleting the app.</p>
  <p>we can't terminate your use (there's no account to terminate).</p>

  <h2>governing law</h2>
  <p>these terms are governed by Delaware law, USA.</p>

  <h2>contact</h2>
  <p>questions: <a href="mailto:hi@beadster.ai">hi@beadster.ai</a></p>
  <p>operated by: System Operator LLC, Delaware, USA.</p>
</Layout>
